                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef327ed1-b140-3fb8-bac2-840d1a7d6aab",
                        "entry_id": "2d739c17-81ef-309c-8ef9-8ecb0edf99f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To show in advance; to foretell, predict."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "03843e6c-3055-4afa-b89b-5a0548a0cc38",
                                "sense_id": "ef327ed1-b140-3fb8-bac2-840d1a7d6aab",
                                "text": "Amid his senses' giddy wheel, / Did he not desperate impulse feel, / Headlong to plunge himself below, / And meet the worst his fears foreshow?— […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6108a162-6e0d-4b28-85d4-c97f91511d62",
                                "sense_id": "ef327ed1-b140-3fb8-bac2-840d1a7d6aab",
                                "text": "What could the soothsayer foreshow that we knew not before? The future is written in the past; and if we prophesy, it is with eyes that look behind."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "40078ae5-6087-3e17-8c5d-4e1d90f8f25e",
                        "entry_id": "2d739c17-81ef-309c-8ef9-8ecb0edf99f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To foreshadow or prefigure."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "865b43cd-86d2-4a21-a5c7-dd49684adc94",
                                "sense_id": "40078ae5-6087-3e17-8c5d-4e1d90f8f25e",
                                "text": "But if the rays break forth out of the middle, or dispersed, and its exterior body, or the out parts of it, be covered with clouds, it foreshows great tempests both of wind and rain."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
